      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Full Contact (1992) represents Hong Kong action cinema at its most explosive, with Ringo Lam directing Chow Yun-fat in a revenge thriller that influenced John Woo's later works. The film revolutionized action cinematography with its \"bullet's eye view\" shots following projectiles through the air. This technique later inspired similar sequences in <a href=\"/movie/603\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"603\">The Matrix</a> (1999) and <a href=\"/movie/8909\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"8909\">Wanted</a> (2008). Lam's raw, gritty direction contrasted sharply with the more stylized approach of his Hong Kong contemporaries, establishing a grittier template for action films."
      },
